## Prerequisites

Before you can make music, you need the TidalCycles stack installed:

### 1. SuperCollider (Audio Engine)

Download and install from: https://supercollider.github.io/downloads

After installing, open SuperCollider and run this to install SuperDirt:
```supercollider
Quarks.checkForUpdates({Quarks.install("SuperDirt", "v1.7.3"); thisProcess.recompile})
```

### 2. Haskell (GHC via ghcup)

Install ghcup (manages Haskell installations):
```bash
curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://get-ghcup.haskell.org | sh
```

Then install GHC and cabal:
```bash
ghcup install ghc 9.6.7
ghcup set ghc 9.6.7
ghcup install cabal latest
```

### 3. TidalCycles

```bash
cabal update
cabal install tidal --lib
```

Full guide: https://tidalcycles.org/docs/getting-started/installation/

### 4. VS Code + TidalCycles Extension (Recommended)

1. Install [VS Code](https://code.visualstudio.com/)
2. Install the [TidalCycles extension](https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=tidalcycles.vscode-tidalcycles)

### 5. Audiomancer (AI Integration)

```bash
pip install audiomancer
# Or from source:
git clone https://github.com/youruser/audiomancer
cd audiomancer && pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

### Verify Installation

```bash
audiomancer doctor
```

This checks that all dependencies are properly installed.

## Quick Start

### First Time Setup

1. **Start SuperCollider audio engine:**
   ```bash
   open -a SuperCollider start_superdirt.scd
   ```
   Wait for "SuperDirt: listening to Tidal on port 57120" in the SuperCollider post window.

2. **Open your session in VS Code:**
   ```bash
   code session.tidal
   ```

3. **Start making sound:**
   - Place cursor on a line of code
   - Press `Shift+Enter` to evaluate that line
   - Press `Ctrl+Enter` to evaluate a block

### Your First Pattern

```haskell
-- Evaluate this line (Shift+Enter):
d1 $ sound "bd bd sn bd"

-- Stop it:
d1 $ silence

-- Stop everything:
hush
```

